# What setup.sh creates here, and what must never enter the repository.
#
# This is the voice directory the host actually runs (vendor-paths.ts points the
# sidecar at it). setup.sh builds a ~1.2 GB virtual environment in .venv/ and
# downloads ~711 MB of open-source engine weights into models/. Both are
# reproducible — from requirements.txt and from MODELS.md — and both would
# otherwise be staged by a plain `git add -A`.
#
# models/aurora-prompt.wav, the clone prompt the sidecar reads, is generated
# too: setup.sh synthesizes it when it is absent, so it is not committed either.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
models/*

